 few other  things to note here the more enemies  your white phantom kills the less time  he has in your world this means the host  will have to do most of the work as I  said before no more crutches you can  still summon help but you'd better pull  your weight this time around now the  next thing invasions in Dark Souls there  were two states hollow and human you  could only be invaded when human in dark  souls - there's no easy way out as long  as you're connected to the net  you can always be invaded whether your  hollow human it doesn't matter you're  vulnerable wherever  go the PvP guys should be really happy  with this one not only do we have proper  servers now but now that everyone is  vulnerable imagine how much easier it  will be to invade the pool of people who  can be invaded should have just  increased dramatically now a few people  actually complain about being invaded  and even go as far as to play offline  but I don't understand those people  being threatened by other players is  part of the experience even if it's  unbalanced at times it's so exciting  trying to progress through a level with  someone in your world trying to kill you  I've never really found any other game  that gives that same adrenaline rush  that you get when someone else invades  you and this goes doubly so for launch  if you've never played a souls game at  launch then you're in for a good time  it's such an amazing experience to  explore with and against other players  who are just as overwhelmed by the game  as you are one last note on this topic  covenants are going to be much more  important this time around one covenant  in particular has leaked it's called the  way of Blu assumedly that's the name in  progress anyway when you join this  covenant when you get invaded by a red  phantom you'll get a blue phantom tasked  with protecting you from the invader the  last piece of news I've got for you guys  is regarding death in Dark Souls 2 and  this is arguably the most major mechanic  change with herds date in Demon Souls  you operated with 50% health if you're  in Sulphur you could restore to human  form and get that health back in Dark  Souls there were 2 States hollow and  human but there was no real gameplay  disadvantage to either of them now in  Dark Souls 2 every time you die as a  hollow you will lose a bit of your  maximum health I imagine it'll work like  this die once that's 10% health less die  again that's 20% health less and so on  and so on until you're left with a  minimum of 50% health to defeat the  level that's your punishment for making  mistakes now in the law hollowing is a  constant process you lose a bit of  humanity every time you die this  mechanic of losing a bit of health every  time you die actually suits the law a  bit more now a while ago from software  express that they were kind of  displeased with her humanity worked in  the original game I mean look at this I  spent hours customizing my waifu and i  end up looking like beef jerky for the  entire game now in Dark Souls 2  according to polygon humanity as an item  seems to be completely removed  apparently you restored a human via a  consumable item called  human effigy an effigy is a sacrifice so  I assume you're sacrificing someone  else's humanity to restore your own law  implications aside I assume that when  you're human you won't lose maximum  health if you're Hollow you'll be  operating at a lower life bar every time  you die and you can restore your health  bar by restoring your humanity I love  this change as well it's a tough but  fair punishment we've dealt with similar  punishments to our health bars and  previous games  you know like curse and soul form but  losing a bit of health each time is more  incremental than losing 50 percent of  your health at once so I assume their  reasoning was that you should be skilled  enough to overcome it as you learn more  about the stage you keep dying in so  those are the major points but I'm not  going to 